      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "Which countries and contexts are you referring to? I feel like there would need to be a really strong use case for this, given the privacy implications. From what I’ve seen, this might not even be an issue... so if you could elaborate, that’d help clear things up!\n\nRight now, 18+ is broad enough that it doesn’t really give useful information to those with bad motives. It doesn’t present much of a risk in terms of cyberstalking, doxxing or targeted predatory behaviour, but does give a general indication of legal adulthood across (nearly all?) countries.\n\nHowever, by adding 21+ above it, you’re making the exact age of anyone under that threshold (18,19,20) much easier to discern. That feels a bit uncomfortable from a privacy and online safety standpoint, as the forced revealing of that information could be beneficial to those who engage in cyberstalking and doxing, or make it easier for predatory types to target inexperienced adults.",
